// Stand-in for the now-UNCONDITIONAL core.cla manifest entry (Plan
// native-5d Task 3) in this fake runtime-module directory (Task 4's
// inclusion-machinery test, internal/lowlevel/rtinc_test.go). Deliberately
// empty, same reason as this directory's str.cla/text.cla/list.cla/map.cla
// stand-ins: this directory exercises expand's declare-before-use splicing
// machinery, not core.cla's real content -- the real module lives at
// runtime/clarus/core.cla. main.cla now always adds "core.cla" to
// neededMods FIRST, regardless of usage flags, so --rtdir
// testdata/rtinc/rt needs SOME file by that name (an empty/decl-less file
// pushes main.cla's own "-1 head" empty-file sentinel, already handled) or
// TestRtInc's IncludesRuntimeModule/NoInclusionWithoutUsage subtests fail
// with "runtime module core.cla not found" before ever reaching the
// assertions they actually care about. Staying empty also preserves
// IncludesRuntimeModule's "clar_fn_rtIncHelper is the first clar_fn_
// symbol" assertion -- core.cla is spliced even before str.cla, but an
// empty stand-in contributes no clar_fn_ symbols of its own.
